From 40a369719a7780fdcfc6deb773103b098c00e9db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:06:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 073/108] gpu: vulkan: plumbing for extended dynamic state
 1/2/3 and graphics pipeline libraries; pairing-independent interpolator
 interface (inactive)

- Device: VK_EXT_extended_dynamic_state3 (polygon mode, depth clamp, colour
  blend enable/equation/write mask, rasterization samples), VK_EXT_graphics_
  pipeline_library + VK_KHR_pipeline_library (fast linking, independent
  interpolation decoration properties), core 1.3 EDS1/EDS2 functions;
  deferred command buffer commands for all of them.
- Translator: SetFixedInterpolatorLocations - interpolator I at location I in
  every stage (others from 16), so shaders translated with different masks link.
- Geometry shader key holds the interpolator mask (dense mask = the old packed
  locations, unchanged behaviour).
- IssueDraw: with UsesCanonicalInterpolatorMasks, the vertex shader exports
  everything it writes and the pixel shader reads its own inputs (the pair's
  intersection only when the VS doesn't cover the PS). Off until the pipeline
  library path lands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

